      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 10, \"items_by_type\": {\"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_1465\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the Provost Area at the School of Science level, excluding the Biology department, and for each organization within those departments (excluding organizations with IDs '138' and '250'), show the department name, department code, organization name, organization ID, the maximum average organization number within each department code group, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the area of rooms assigned to the organization (considering only organizations with more than 5 rooms and excluding organizations named 'ADMISSIONS'), ordered by department name and organization name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3890\", \"desc\": \"For each major use description, list the building-room identifier, area, major use description, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the major use description, as well as the organization name, department name, department code, department long name, department level, and the average organization number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the organization parent, ordered by the organization name, but only include those organizations whose organization number is greater than the average organization number of their parent group. For each major use description, include a grand total row for all rooms in the format of (null, null, major use description, total rooms) and only include rooms whose organization matches the filtered organizations. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4776\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with an area greater than 300 that are associated with departments in the \\\"Provost Area\\\", show the building-room identifier, floor number, major use description, organization name, DLC key, the average area in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department code and ordered by area, the department code, department name, school area name, and the rank of each department within its school area based on department code. Additionally, include the department's full name from the HR organization unit and the department's hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy. Present the results ordered by building-room identifier and department code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4061\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, show the department name, academic year, academic year description, and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered by the department in regular terms with total units greater than zero, along with, for each academic building where these subjects are held and which has rooms larger than 40 square meters, the building name, the average, range, and variance of the room areas, as well as the total assignable area of the building and the year the building was built. The results are ordered by department name, academic year (descending), and room area range (descending). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1833\", \"desc\": \"For each department and subject grade type where the subject is offered in the current academic year, is letter graded, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of subjects, the minimum total units, the school name, the department phone number, the organization name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the department's DLC name, including subtotals for each department (the corresponding department field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all departments (the corresponding department field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the department if it is the same as the previous row. Only include organizations that have more than 5 rooms, are associated with a non-null DLC key, and are not the 'ADMISSIONS' department or the 'Political Science' department. Sort the table by department, grade type, and descending standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of room areas. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3490\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" with a non-null department code, show the department name, the department's long name, the corresponding hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the department name, and for each matching space unit with a space unit key greater than 100000, show the space unit code, the organization name, the HR department name from the space unit, and the sum of space unit keys within each warehouse load date group ordered by space unit key. Present the results ordered by department name and space unit code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1350\", \"desc\": \"For each department and school, provide the department name, school name, the average, range, and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, and the total enrolled students, considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with at least one enrolled student. Additionally, for each school, include a grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (null department name, school name, nulls for statistics, and total enrolled students). For students whose first name is 'Peter' and who are in the Mathematics department, also show their last name, email address, student year, and the minimum department budget code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's full name, as well as the department full name and department last activity date. The results include all these columns in the following order: department name, school name, average enrolled students, range of enrolled students, variance of enrolled students, total enrolled students, last name, email address, student year, windowed minimum department budget code, department full name, and department last activity date. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4452\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" that is associated with a space unit with space unit code 97500, show the department code, department name, school area name, the rank of each department within its school area based on department code, the corresponding DLC name, the space unit name, space unit code, associated organization name, department count, number of supervisees, and the highest research volume ever recorded for each department count group. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2224\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code where the department is degree granting and the department is Mathematics, and for each department that is degree granting and is not the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject code, subject code description, mathematics department name, school name, the average department budget code within each school, the administrative department name, the average clearing cost collector, the variance of the clearing cost collector, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the clearing cost collector, and the most recent activity date for the administrative department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1888\", \"desc\": \"For each academic building in Cambridge, MA (excluding the Stata building), with more than 1 room and a non-null building name, and that is also an academic building at MIT with more than 10 rooms, show the building key, building name, building type, the number of historical records, the total assignable area across all historical records, the average number of rooms per historical record, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the total assignable area of the building at MIT, 