      "content": "The MySQL connection is consistently returning \"Access denied\" (an infrastructure issue, not a query issue), so I cannot execute verification queries. I'll complete the analysis based on the semantic network evidence and submit the best-supported SQL.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (investigated):**\n- **FCLT_ROOMS** — facilities room inventory, one row per physical room. Key columns: `AREA` (\"Room area in square meters; used in area statistics (average, range, variance)\"), `DEPT_CODE` (\"Department code assigned to the room\"), `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY`, `FCLT_ROOM_KEY`.\n- **FCLT_ORGANIZATION** — facilities organization dimension (levels 1–6), with `DLC_KEY`/`DLC_NAME`, `COURSE` (academic course number), `ORGANIZATION_NAME`. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` for room occupancy attribution.\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — academic department dimension: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (canonical name), full name, school attribution, `DLC_KEY`.\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — catalog-level subject offering per academic year/term: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS`, `TERM_CODE`, `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`, `MEET_PLACE` (→ FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ROOM_KEY).\n- **SUBJECT_SUMMARY** — registrar subject-level summary per term with `DEPARTMENT_CODE/NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS`, enrollment statistics.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS** — term dimension with `TERM_CODE` and `IS_REGULAR_TERM` ('Y'/'N', \"regular term (Fall/Spring) versus non-regular terms (Summer, January/IAP); only present in ACADEMIC_TERMS, not in ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\").\n\n**Column concepts:** `column_concept_total_units` (decision guide: \"Unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance/geometric mean) over catalog offerings → use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\"); `column_concept_department_name` (decision guide: \"Joining fact tables to department dimension attributes → prefer code joins: DEPARTMENT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"); `column_concept_term_code` (universal term join key).\n\n**Concepts:** `concept_room_space_inventory`, `concept_department_dimension`, `concept_subject_offering_facts`, `concept_academic_term_dimension`.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- FCLT_ROOMS joins: FCLT_BUILDING, FCLT_ORGANIZATION, FCLT_MAJOR_USE, FCLT_FLOOR, SPACE_UNIT, FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY; incoming from COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (MEET_PLACE = FCLT_ROOM_KEY). 16 metrics depend on it.\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT joins (graph): COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY/SUBJECT_OFFERED(_SUMMARY), TIP/LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, FCLT_ORGANIZATION — all via department codes.\n- Precedent lineages retrieved: dw_4061 (ACADEMIC_TERMS + COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED + FCLT_ROOMS/FCLT_BUILDING), dw_4387 (TERM_CODE join with IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y'), dw_1049 (SUBJECT_SUMMARY + ACADEMIC_TERMS regular term), dw_1833/dw_1465/dw_3332/dw_4776 (room area stats via FCLT_ROOMS; DEPT_CODE used directly from FCLT_ROOMS in dw_3332/dw_4776).\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Room-area source candidates:**\n| Dimension | FCLT_ROOMS.DEPT_CODE | FCLT_ROOMS→FCLT_ORGANIZATION | SPACE_DETAIL→SPACE_UNIT |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | one row per room (evidence: table def) | one row per room, org dimension | one row per room-space unit |\n| \"Assigned to department\" match | `DEPT_CODE` desc = \"Department code assigned to the room\" — exact lexical match | organization occupancy attribution (indirect) | space-unit allocation (indirect) |\n| Area column | `AREA` in m², explicitly \"used in area statistics (average, range, variance)\" | same AREA | square footage (different unit) |\n| Precedent | dw_3332, dw_4776 partition/select FCLT_ROOMS.DEPT_CODE directly | dw_1833, dw_1465 (org-level stddev) | dw_4025 |\n\n**3b. Total-units source candidates:** COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS (catalog; decision guide names it for \"avg/stddev/variance\" unit statistics; used by dw_4061/dw_4387 for regular terms) vs SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS (registrar; used by dw_1049). Task requirement \"subjects offered in regular academic terms\" + \"average, range, variance of total units\" → both SUPPORTED; catalog table is the one whose decision guide entry covers variance-style statistics and which carries DEPARTMENT_CODE joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.\n\n**3c. Wording anchoring:** \"rooms assigned to it [the department]\" anchors to FCLT_ROOMS.DEPT_CODE (\"Department code assigned to the room\"); \"area greater than 40\" → `AREA > 40` (dw_4061 precedent uses exactly `r.AREA > 40`); \"regular academic terms\" → `ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'` (only ACADEMIC_TERMS has this column); \"department name\" → canonical SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME (per exact-SELECT discipline, no variants).\n\n**3d. Precedent usage:** regular-term join on TERM_CODE: dw_4387 (`c.TERM_CODE = t.TERM_CODE`, IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y'); on EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE: dw_4061, dw_359. \"Offered in\" a term semantically matches the offering TERM_CODE (dw_4387's wording \"offered in regular academic terms\" is nearly identical to this task). Room-area AVG/MAX−MIN/VARIANCE pattern: dw_4061 (`AVG(r.AREA)`, `MAX(r.AREA)-MIN(r.AREA)`, `VARIANCE(r.AREA)`).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nFCLT_ROOMS serves room-size dispersion analytics (16 metrics). COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED + ACADEMIC_TERMS serves per-department unit statistics in regular terms (dw_4061, dw_4387, dw_359). SIS_DEPARTMENT is the canonical name resolver joined by code.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nInvestigated: FCLT_ROOMS, FCLT_ORGANIZATION, SIS_DEPARTMENT, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, ACADEMIC_TERMS (semantic_get); concepts/column_concepts above (semantic_get/search); metrics dw_4061, dw_1833, dw_4776, dw_1465, dw_1049, dw_4387, dw_359, dw_3332, dw_4271, dw_3890 (trace_lineage/semantic_get); graph neighbors for FCLT_ROOMS, SIS_DEPARTMENT; metrics_by_table FCLT_ROOMS. mysql_query attempted 7 times — all failed with server-side \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\", so data verification was impossible; this is noted explicitly.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n**6a.** FCLT_ROOMS (`AREA`, `DEPT_CODE`) for room stats with `AREA > 40`; COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (`TOTAL_UNITS`, `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `TERM_CODE`) joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS (`IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y'`) for unit stats; SIS_DEPARTMENT for the canonical `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, joined by code on both sides.\n**6b.** Two aggregated CTEs at department-code granularity, then join both to SIS_DEPARTMENT — this avoids any fan-out between the room and subject populations. Range = MAX−MIN, variance = VARIANCE(), no rounding.\n**6c.** Data: DEPT_CODE is documented as the room's assigned department code and AREA is documented for exactly these statistics; code joins are the documented reliable path. Semantic-network: dw_4061/dw_4387 precedents use the same tables, filters, and aggregate forms. Business: matches the \"per-department space + curriculum profile\" question pattern.\n**6d.** Alternative: SUBJECT_SUMMARY for units (dw_1049 precedent) or EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE join (dw_4061); TERM_CODE + catalog table chosen because the task wording \"subjects offered in regular academic terms\" matches dw_4387's near-identical phrasing.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
